%I A056163 #27 Sep 09 2026 01:26:46
%S A056163 2,3,5,11,120,191297,9223767764448107,
%T A056163 11156067073141567281944337164803427449
%N A056163 Number of ordered antichains on an unlabeled n-set; labeled T_1-hypergraphs with n hyperedges.
%C A056163 A T_1-hypergraph is a hypergraph (not necessarily without empty hyperedges or multiple hyperedges) which for every ordered pair of distinct nodes has a hyperedge containing one but not the other node.
%C A056163 If a permutation of [n] has j cycles, then its invariant subsets are exactly the unions of these cycles, hence form a Boolean lattice B_j. Therefore the number of fixed ordered antichains is F(j), and Burnside's lemma gives the formula below. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 07 2026
%D A056163 Vladeta Jovovic and Goran Kilibarda, On the number of Boolean functions in the Post classes F^{mu}_8, Diskretnaya Matematika, 11 (1999), no. 4, 127-138 (translated in Discrete Mathematics and Applications, 9, (1999), no. 6)
%D A056163 Vladeta Jovovic and Goran Kilibarda, On enumeration of the class of all monotone Boolean functions, in preparation.
%H A056163 K. S. Brown, <a href="http://www.mathpages.com/home/kmath515.htm">Dedekind's problem</a>
%H A056163 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Cover.html">Antichain covers</a>
%F A056163 a(n) = Sum_{k=0..C(n, floor(n/2))} b(k, n) where b(k, n) is the number of k-element ordered antichains on an unlabeled n-set.
%F A056163 Let D(n,k) = A059119(n,k), and F(n) = Sum_{k>=0} k!*D(n,k). Then a(n) = (1/n!)*Sum_{j=0..n} Stirling1(n,j)*F(j), where Stirling1(n,j) denotes the unsigned Stirling number of the first kind and F(n) = A037843(n). - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 07 2026
%F A056163 a(n) = 2 + Sum_{k=1..n} A056164(k). - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 08 2026
%e A056163 a(1) = 1+2 = 3.
%e A056163 a(2) = 1+3+1 = 5.
%e A056163 a(3) = 1+4+4+2 = 11.
%e A056163 a(4) = 1+5+10+19+25+30+30 = 120.
%e A056163 There are 11 ordered antichains on an unlabeled 3-set: 0, (0), ({1}), ({1,2}), ({1,2,3}), ({1},{2}), ({1},{2,3}), ({2,3},{1}), ({1,2},{1,3}), ({1},{2},{3}), ({1,2},{1,3},{2,3}).
%Y A056163 Cf. A000372 for (unordered) antichains on a labeled n-set, A056005, A056069-A056071, A056073, A056046-A056049, A056052, A056101, A056104, A051112-A051118, A037843, A059119, A056164, A399696.
%K A056163 nonn,hard,more,changed
%O A056163 0,1
%A A056163 _Vladeta Jovovic_ and Goran Kilibarda, Jul 31 2000
